{% comment %}
  Custom robots.txt — added 2026-09-19.

  Renders Shopify's default groups unchanged, then blocks the SEO-intelligence
  crawlers. Those exist to sell competitor analysis of this store; they bring no
  traffic and no customers, and they are a share of the bot load that made the
  client-error log 81% noise.

  DELIBERATELY NOT BLOCKED:
    - Googlebot / Bingbot / Applebot — search.
    - facebookexternalhit, meta-externalads, Twitterbot, etc. — link previews and
      ad review. Blocking these breaks how shared links and ads render.
    - GPTBot / ClaudeBot / PerplexityBot / CCBot — AI assistants. GA4 already
      shows a small "AI Assistant" referral channel and it is likely to grow;
      blocking them trades future visibility for nothing measurable today.

  Only well-behaved crawlers obey robots.txt. This is tidying, not defence — the
  storefront is on Shopify, so there is no firewall layer available to us.

  NOTE: creating this template replaces Shopify's generated file. If Shopify's
  agent-commerce preamble (UCP/MCP endpoints, shop.app skill, "checkouts are for
  humans") is missing from the live /robots.txt after deploying this, delete this
  file and push again to fall back to the default — the preamble is worth more
  than these four blocks.
{% endcomment %}
{% for group in robots.default_groups %}
  {{- group.user_agent }}

  {% for rule in group.rules -%}
    {{ rule }}
  {% endfor -%}

  {%- if group.sitemap != blank -%}
    {{ group.sitemap }}
  {% endif -%}
{% endfor %}

